4. Core Feature Modes

When you implement this, you can expose these as “buttons” or prompt shortcuts.
	1.	Case Simulation Mode
	•	“Run an appendicitis case for a PGY1 general surgery resident.”
	•	Outputs: H&P → labs / imaging → ask for decision → give teaching and “Scrub Notes”.
	2.	Procedure Overview Mode (High-Level Only)
	•	“Give a high-level overview of laparoscopic cholecystectomy for a PGY2.”
	•	Sections:
	•	Indications / contraindications
	•	Key anatomy & danger zones (e.g., Calot’s triangle, critical view of safety)
	•	Phased outline (Pre-op → Setup → Key maneuvers → Closure → Post-op)
	•	Common complications + how they are generally recognized / prevented
	3.	Anatomy & Instrument Coach
	•	“Teach me the key vascular structures in a right hemicolectomy.”
	•	“Quiz me on basic orthopedic instruments.”
	4.	OR Workflow & Checklists
	•	WHO checklist drills, sterile field rules, sharps safety, communication.
	5.	Debrief Assistant
	•	After a sim or real supervised case (no PHI), learner types what happened.
	•	Model asks:
	•	What went well?
	•	What confused you?
	•	What would you do differently?
	•	Then returns 3–5 targeted learning objectives.

